---@class aws.route53globalresolver.CreateFirewallRuleInput
---@field action aws.route53globalresolver.FirewallRuleAction|string The action that DNS Firewall should take on a DNS query when it matches one of the domains in the rule's domain list:
---@field blockOverrideDnsType? aws.route53globalresolver.BlockOverrideDnsQueryType|string The DNS record's type. This determines the format of the record value that you provided in BlockOverrideDomain. Used for the rule action BLOCK with a BlockResponse setting of OVERRIDE.
---@field blockOverrideDomain? aws.route53globalresolver.Domain The custom DNS record to send back in response to the query. Used for the rule action BLOCK with a BlockResponse setting of OVERRIDE.
---@field blockOverrideTtl? aws.route53globalresolver.BlockOverrideTtl The recommended amount of time, in seconds, for the DNS resolver or web browser to cache the provided override record. Used for the rule action BLOCK with a BlockResponse setting of OVERRIDE.
---@field blockResponse? aws.route53globalresolver.FirewallBlockResponse|string The response to return when the action is BLOCK. Valid values are NXDOMAIN (domain does not exist), NODATA (domain exists but no records), or OVERRIDE (return custom response).
---@field clientToken? aws.route53globalresolver.ClientToken A unique, case-sensitive identifier to ensure idempotency. This means that making the same request multiple times with the same clientToken has the same result every time.
---@field confidenceThreshold? aws.route53globalresolver.ConfidenceThreshold|string The confidence threshold for advanced threat detection. Valid values are HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW, indicating the accuracy level required for threat detection.
---@field description? aws.route53globalresolver.ResourceDescription An optional description for the firewall rule.
---@field dnsAdvancedProtection? aws.route53globalresolver.DnsAdvancedProtection|string Whether to enable advanced DNS threat protection for this rule. Advanced protection can detect and block DNS tunneling and Domain Generation Algorithm (DGA) threats.
---@field firewallDomainListId? aws.route53globalresolver.ResourceId The ID of the firewall domain list to use in this rule.
---@field name aws.route53globalresolver.ResourceName A descriptive name for the firewall rule.
---@field priority? aws.route53globalresolver.FirewallRulePriority The priority of this rule. Rules are evaluated in priority order, with lower numbers having higher priority. When a DNS query matches multiple rules, the rule with the highest priority (lowest number) is applied.
---@field dnsViewId aws.route53globalresolver.ResourceId The ID of the DNS view to associate with this firewall rule.
